  "limitations": [
    "Survivorship bias: the live universe is 21 companies alive today plus 4 ETFs. A point-in-time test including delisted stocks (research/massive, M2) did not reach DSR 0.95.",
    "History is Massive's rolling 10-year window (it starts in late 2016 and moves forward daily): the 2008 crisis is not tested.",
    "GARCH and HMM parameters are refitted once a year using only earlier data (point-in-time); the first 500 sessions are training only and are never traded.",
    "The per-asset HMM can switch between two near-equally likely fits as data arrives; only the market (SPY) regime gates trading, and it is stable.",
    "Daily bars only: no volume bars, order book or intraday sessions.",
    "Trades enter at the next session's open and barriers use intraday highs/lows, exactly like the paper ledger; a day that touches both counts as the stop.",
    "With few trials the DSR is close to a Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio against zero."
  ],
